# [DTN](../wg/dtn.html)

## Summary

The DTN Working Group met at IETF 127 for its second session of the week. The agenda covered updates on active working group drafts, individual contributions, field demonstration results, and proposals for working group adoption. Key topics included:

- Updates on the Manifest Extension Block and BP Safe pairwise key exchange protocol.
- Protocol refinements and implementation status of [draft-ietf-dtn-btpu](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dtn-btpu/) and [draft-ietf-dtn-btpu-fec](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dtn-btpu-fec/).
- High-throughput (2 Gbps) field demonstration results of BTPU over a free-space optical link by Eleria using the Hardy Bundle Protocol Agent (BPA) and [draft-ietf-dtn-bibe](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dtn-bibe/).
- Multicast endpoint addressing via the IMC URI scheme (`imc:`).
- Mapping HTTP request/response payloads over Bundle Protocol for REST services and web distribution.
- The SPAM framework for BPsec integrity protection against arbitrary packet dropping.
- CCSDS Custody Transfer, Compressed Bundle Status Reporting, and Bundle Sequence Identification specifications.
- Design options for adding bundle aggregation to [draft-ietf-dtn-bibe](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dtn-bibe/).
- Reverse DNS lookups for IPN endpoints using the `ipn.arpa` domain.

